#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:11
msgid "Complete an eCommerce payment using Taler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:13
msgid ""
"Once you have completed the Taler initial setup, customers can pay on "
"your website."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:15
msgid "To do so, they will open the shop and add any items to their cart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:16
msgid "During the checkout, they can now select the ``Taler`` payment provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid "Taler eCommerce checkout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid ".. image:: ../images/EN/Taler_ecommerce_checkout.png"
msgstr ".. image:: ../images/FR/Taler_ecommerce_checkout.png"

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:24
msgid ""
"After clicking ``Pay now``, a new Taler order will be created on the "
"merchant side, and the customer will be redirected to the Taler order, "
"from which they can pay with any Taler wallet on their phone or web "
"browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid "Taler eCommerce wallet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid ".. image:: ../images/EN/Taler_ecommerce_wallet.png"
msgstr ".. image:: ../images/FR/Taler_ecommerce_wallet.png"

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:34
msgid ""
"Upon completion of the payment using their wallet, the customer will be "
"redirected back to your Odoo website, which will show a successful "
"payment confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid "Taler eCommerce payment processor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid ".. image:: ../images/EN/Taler_ecommerce_payment_processed.png"
msgstr ".. image:: ../images/FR/Taler_ecommerce_payment_processed.png"

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:46
msgid "Purchase an Event ticket online using Taler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:50
msgid ""
"To have a fully working ticketing system, you might need to install the "
"python module pycairo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:52
msgid "``sudo apt install libcairo2-dev``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:53
msgid "``pip install rlPyCairo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:55
msgid "To make event tickets available for customers to pay using Taler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:57
msgid "Add the ``Events`` add-on on your Odoo instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:58
msgid "Go to the settings app, and navigate to the ``Events`` settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:59
msgid "Tick the ``Online Ticketing`` setting and save the changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid "Taler ticketing settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid ".. image:: ../images/EN/Taler_ticketing_settings.png"
msgstr ".. image:: ../images/FR/Taler_ticketing_settings.png"

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:66
msgid ""
"Tickets will now be available to buy using online payments providers, "
"including the Taler payment provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:68
msgid ""
"Customers can navigate the ``Events`` tab on your website, and choose a "
"ticket to any event they’re interested in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid "Taler ticketing event list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:-1
msgid ".. image:: ../images/EN/Taler_ticketing_events_list.png"
msgstr ".. image:: ../images/FR/Taler_ticketing_events_list.png"

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:76
msgid ""
"Upon clicking an event, they will be asked to provide some identifying "
"information, and then will be lead to a payment page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:78
msgid "On this payment page, the customer can select Taler as a payment provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:80
msgid ""
"They will be redirected to a Taler order page, where they can pay using "
"their Taler wallet on the app or web browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/payments.rst:82
msgid ""
"Once the payment is completed, the customer will land back on the odoo "
"page, with their payment successfully processed, and a .pdf of the event "
"tickets available."
msgstr ""

